      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the late 1870s, the Franklin and Pittsylvania Railroad built a depot right beside the post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.victorianvilla.com/sims-mitchell/local/articles/phsp/055/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "That depot was later converted into a World War II prisoner‑of‑war camp, adding a dramatic chapter to the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.victorianvilla.com/sims-mitchell/local/articles/phsp/055/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Throughout its 153‑year history, the Sandy Level post office served 24 different postmasters.",
